    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28143" root="عجز" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُجْزٌ</span></b>  <i>Old age</i> of a woman: a simple subst.
(TA.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِتَّقِى ٱللّٰهَ فِى شَبِيبَتِكِ وَعُجْزِكِ</span>
<i>Fear thou God in thy youth and</i> [<i>thine old age,</i>
or] <i>when thou becomest an old woman.</i> (TA.
[But <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتّق</span> is there put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِتَّقِى</span>: and in the
explanation, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَصِيرُ</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَصِيرِينَ</span>. See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجَزَتْ</span>.]) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجُزٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجِزَتْ</span>.]

